:'''Jing Yuan:''' The Astral Express! I must confess that the train's reputation precedes it, such that it is often close to my thoughts. How delightful to come face to face with its passengers!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Frightfully delightful!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Would that this occasion had come sooner!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...Are you really a general?
:'''Welt:''' It's an honor to meet you, general. May I ask what the favor you spoke of is?
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Ah, a matter that requires capable people such as yourselves. We captured a member of the Stellaron Hunters a few days ago, who goes by the name of "Blade."
:'''Jing Yuan:''' During our investigation, the Divination Commission &mdash; the department in charge of intelligence processing &mdash; intercepted a transmission sent out by his accomplice, Kafka, who has managed to hide aboard the ship. As for where that transmission was destined...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The Express.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Go on! Where!?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:'''Welt:''' ...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' I have some knowledge of your relationship with the Stellaron Hunters. The Divination Commission is convinced that you made an alliance with them... I say that's impossible. The crew of the Astral Express are honorable people whose valiant deeds are lauded across the universe. There must have been a misunderstanding.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' As such, I came to the conclusion that the communication must have been an attempt by the Stellaron Hunters to sow dissent between us.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's right! We've been framed!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe the Stellaron Hunters have other motives...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' We can handle the Stellaron, but it will take time and will require the bulk of the Cloud Knights on the ship. It is this Kafka that concerns me. The longer she stays on the ship, the bigger the threat she will pose.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Since the Stellaron Hunters lured you to our ship, we shall move with the current. You are hereby authorized to do as you deem fit on the Luofu, with the goal of bringing Kafka out of the shadows and under our control.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Doing so would clear the misunderstanding between us, reveal the true intentions of the Stellaron Hunters, and help us understand their connection to the Stellaron burst. What say you, my Astral guests?
:'''Welt:''' ...(Trailblazer), what do you think?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's move with the current and help out.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' If you are able to capture this Stellaron Hunter, the Xianzhou will be indebted to you.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Our expedition was focused on the Stellaron...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' I'm afraid my hands are tied on the matter &mdash; this is a diplomatic affair and I have rules to follow. But if you can bring me the Stellaron Hunter and discover her motive for placing a Stellaron on the ship, it would be of great help in resolving the incident.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We don't really have a choice.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Of course you do. You can be strangers and simply walk away. But I feel you wish to help the Xianzhou.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' The Luofu never fails to reward that which is given.
:'''Welt:''' ...Okay.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Wonderful, it's a deal then. I shall notify Yukong that all intel is to be shared with you, and that our best personnel are to aid you in your search.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' If there's anything the Sky-Faring Commission or the Cloud Knights can do for you during your stay, don't hesitate to make it known.
:The chat concluded, and Welt shot you a covert gesture. You understand that this is the Crew's own discussion time.
----

;(Talk to Yukong)
:'''Yukong:''' Seeing as the general gave the order, the Sky-Faring Commission will lend you our full support. The Stellaron Hunter investigation is in your hands now. I'll issue you a pass so you can access the facilities around Starskiff Haven.
:'''Yukong:''' As for personnel... the skyports are currently all under maintenance, so we're thinly stretched. What I can do is send Tingyun as your guide &mdash; she'll take care of you during your stay.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Discuss your conclusions with Welt{{subst:void|<!--102030112-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Palace of Astrum|update|In the Palace of Astrum, the hopeful Trailblazers are unfortunately rejected by Yukong.<br />The Stellaron's descent on the Xianzhou involves many secrets, and Yukong does not wish to employ outsiders to solve such problems. Just as you leave empty-handed, General Jing Yuan of Luofu's Cloud Knights appears and intervenes.<br />This smiling general seems to be on your side and opens a convenient door, but he secretly has other ideas in mind.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Welt Yang)
:'''Welt:''' Hmm, I think we only scratched the surface of this General Jing Yuan...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do you think there's something strange about him?
::'''Welt:''' I don't know about "strange," but my gut tells me something is off.
::'''Welt:''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He seems suspicious...
::'''Welt:''' Oh? Care to elaborate?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why would he stop us from investigating the Stellaron?
:::'''Welt:''' He says he doesn't want outsiders getting involved in the Xianzhou's internal affairs, which is understandable.
:::'''Welt:''' ...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why did he ask us to go after Kafka?
:::'''Welt:''' Yes! There's something about this point...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why is he being so kind to us?
:::'''Welt:''' He wants us to trust him. He took advantage of Yukong's frosty reception to play the good guy.
:::'''Welt:''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I thought he was on our side?
::'''Welt:''' Theoretically, yes. But something feels off.
::'''Welt:''' ...
:'''Welt:''' Ah, that's it! A minor detail, but curious. He avoided talking about Blade!
:'''Welt:''' Since the Cloud Knights have already captured a Stellaron Hunter, why not use him to get to Kafka? Why rely on us?
:'''Welt:''' The Xianzhou is reluctant to involve outsiders in the Stellaron disaster, so why is it so keen on letting us capture a Stellaron Hunter?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Could Blade have escaped?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do you think Jing Yuan lied about the Stellaron?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He's using us as bait...
:'''Welt:''' Yes. The only sensible conclusion I can draw is that Blade had already escaped when Jing Yuan spoke to us &mdash; provided they even captured him in the first place.
:'''Welt:''' Therefore, given our connection to Kafka, we represent the only way of luring the Stellaron Hunters in.
:'''Welt:''' That's why he asked for our help... He didn't want to let anyone else find out that Blade had already escaped!
:'''Welt:''' Now that we've figured that out, perhaps we can get closer to the core of what's happening here.

;(Talk to March 7th)
:'''March 7th:''' We've got a Xianzhou general on our side! This time we have to... wait, does this seem familiar to you? Let's hope he doesn't offer us a hotel!

;(Talk to Jing Yuan's Hologram)
:'''Jing Yuan:''' I have heard of you, (Trailblazer)... The Alliance is very interested in the Astral Express.
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Blade...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Blade is wanted by both the IPC and the Alliance. I'm afraid I cannot comment on his file.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} About Kafka...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' There are five known members of the Stellaron Hunters. Elio is their leader, but always stays behind the scenes. Most of the operations are led by Kafka.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Had the Divination Commission not intercepted her encrypted transmission, she would have remained undetected for much longer.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Once we catch the Stellaron Hunter...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Bring her to us.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Kafka is good at controlling the people around her.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Kafka won't say anything.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' Hmm, ordinary means may prove futile when it comes to this individual. But the Divination Commission has ways of...
::'''Jing Yuan:''' ...Haha, don't misunderstand me. The Xianzhou does not engage in torture. Retrieving intel does not necessarily involve the use of violence.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' In any case, you can deliver her directly to us. Once we learn something, I will share every piece of information with you.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't have any other questions.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' If things go as planned, I would love to find the time to sit with all of you and hear about your experiences among the stars. My responsibilities to the Xianzhou have meant that I haven't had the chance to travel in many years.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' We had heard nothing of the Express for a long time. It is heartening to learn of its continued journey along that starward track.
::'''Jing Yuan:''' I have other matters to attend to. Goodbye for now.
{{Dialogue End}}

