===Go with Tingyun to the Petrichor Inn{{subst:void|<!--102030113-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:{{tx}}
:'''March 7th:''' *yawn* Well, here we are. I feel sleepy already.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The sun hasn't gone down yet.
::'''March 7th:''' What? But we've done a whole day's work &mdash; what's the sun playing at? It felt like we spent the whole day in the Palace of Astrum.
::Ready for a nap? That's not like you, March...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Ready for a nap? That's not like you, March...
:'''March 7th:''' Hey, that's not fair! My eyes are peeled this time &mdash; I'll make a run for it the second things go wrong.
:'''March 7th:''' Jokes aside, did you see Madam Yukong frown at us? I thought her guards were about to jump out of nowhere and throw us in jail.
:'''March 7th:''' *sigh* I'd rather deal with monsters than these big shots...
:'''March 7th:''' Ah! I&mdash;I mean... not that Madam Yukong doesn't have her merits, hehe...
:'''Tingyun:''' Don't worry, my lips are sealed~
:'''Tingyun:''' But as her subordinate, I have to say that it's Madam Yukong's duty to keep her guard up. The Luofu is facing a crisis, and as head of the Sky-Faring Commission, she is responsible for the security of the Xianzhou's customs and borders.
:'''Tingyun:''' She's actually a very reasonable old girl in private.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Old girl?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Reasonable? Are we thinking of the same person?
:'''Tingyun:''' They say that many years ago, Madam Yukong was an ace pilot in the Cloud Knights. She was a "work hard, play harder" type, known for her hot temper and incredible skill.
:'''Tingyun:''' Eventually, she became the head of the entire commission, which required her to learn patience and adopt a meticulous approach to her work.
:'''Tingyun:''' In any case, Madam Yukong instructed me to reserve the best rooms at the inn and have all your expenses covered. She wants to extend the full courtesy of the Xianzhou so that all of you enjoy your stay to the fullest~
:'''Tingyun:''' She specifically mentioned that if you wish to buy anything at the inn, be it food or otherwise, just let the innkeeper know. The commission will cover the cost.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Say thanks to Madam Yukong for us!
::'''March 7th:''' Why don't you go back yourself?
::The commission will cover the cost!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The commission will cover the cost!
:'''March 7th:''' That's the friendliest thing I've heard since we arrived!
:'''March 7th:''' Ahem! S&mdash;Seeing as our hosts are so thoughtful, I guess we should help ourselves. Right, Mr. Yang?
:'''Welt:''' We should focus on our objective first. Seeing as Helm Master Yukong was extremely reluctant to get us involved, am I right to speculate that the Sky-Faring Commission has some leads on the whereabouts of Kafka?
:'''Tingyun:''' Exactly right. The suspect is extremely cunning. She encrypted her transmission and timed her communication &mdash; we couldn't pinpoint her exact location.
:'''Tingyun:''' But as cunning as she is, the Divination Commission has managed to find something.
:'''Kafka:''' Here are the coordinates. It's up to you how to proceed.
:'''Kafka:''' Our destinations may differ, but the orbits of the stars will eventually converge. See you later.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Is there anything special about what she said?
::'''Tingyun:''' Don't let her words distract you.
::Coordinates? Converge?
::'''Tingyun:''' Don't let her words distract you.
::I heard something in the background.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Coordinates? Converge?
::'''Tingyun:''' Don't let her words distract you.
::I heard something in the background.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I heard something in the background.
:'''Tingyun:''' Precisely.
:'''Tingyun:''' That's the sound of a device.
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

