;(Talk to Tingyun)
:'''Tingyun:''' How can I help?
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} There's something I want to say.
::'''Tingyun:''' Oh? Let's hear it.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Was it raining when Kafka's transmission was intercepted?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Kafka was holding an umbrella in her transmission...
::'''Tingyun:''' How perceptive. Our wind, clouds, rain, and fog are all artificial. The Realm-Keeping Commission's weather pavilion manages the environmental conditions here.
::'''Tingyun:''' If Kafka was holding an umbrella, that means she was in an area with artificial rainfall during the transmission.
::'''Tingyun:''' Still, that doesn't help us much. The ship is huge, with changing conditions across various delves. I'm sure there were showers across many of them at the time.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Any chance Kafka is still at Stargazer Navalia?
::'''Tingyun:''' Impossible to say. It used to be that the Divination Commission could track the access history of all the delves...
::'''Tingyun:''' But with the arrival of the Stellaron, things have become messy. Some delves even had their entrance marked as the exit.
::'''Tingyun:''' If I were one of the Stellaron Hunters, I'd be very happy to capitalize on all the chaos. It'd be harder to escape, but easier to blend in.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} Never mind...
----
:'''March 7th:''' Message not sent? Why not?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't know.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Bad signal?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Maybe they demolished the base stations?
:'''Welt:''' Long-range communication technology is still improving. Perhaps the presence of the Stellaron is affecting signal transmission.
:'''March 7th:''' Doesn't seem like it, everything else is working fine &mdash; see?
:'''Welt:''' In that case, it looks like someone wants to make things difficult for us. Since Kafka's here, I wouldn't be surprised if this turns out to be that Stellaron Hunter hacker girl's handiwork.
